Speed: the ML size inliner only for cold code, LLVM's own for the rest.

patches/1008 lets Linux and macOS inline with the model trained for size
(use_ml_inliner). At link time it decides for the whole engine, the hot
code of layout, style and the DOM bindings too, where it keeps small
functions out of line: Blink compiled at -O2 still lost calls that Chrome
inlines. High-end Android builds tell the advisor to use the model only
where the caller is cold in the PGO profile (-ml-inliner-skip-policy=
if-caller-not-cold); a GN argument, zebkit_ml_inliner_cold_cutoff, does
the same here, and sets where cold begins (-profile-summary-cutoff-cold,
in millionths of the profile's counts; 0 leaves the model everywhere).

Measured on Linux slim, 2026-11-02, 900000 beside 0: libzebkit.so.1
9.7 MB larger (+6.6%, +5.7% of the package); 20,000 rows built and laid
out 9% faster (tests/bench/index.html's dom, 406 to 370 ms), style 19%,
DOM bindings 21%; a chapter of text laid out 4% faster. 999999 gave the
same for 13.9 MB, 990000 for 10.9 MB.

--- a/build/config/compiler/compiler.gni
+++ b/build/config/compiler/compiler.gni
@@ -234,6 +234,13 @@
   # Currently the ML inliner is only supported on linux hosts
   use_ml_inliner = host_os == "linux" && is_android
 
+  # zebkit: with use_ml_inliner, the size model decides only where the
+  # caller is cold in the PGO profile, LLVM's own inliner everywhere else.
+  # 0 leaves the model deciding everywhere. Otherwise, the share of the
+  # profile's counts, in millionths, that code above the cold line takes:
+  # LLVM's -profile-summary-cutoff-cold, 999999 by default.
+  zebkit_ml_inliner_cold_cutoff = 0
+
   # Whether we should consider the profile we're using to be accurate. Accurate
   # profiles have the benefit of (potentially substantial) binary size
   # reductions, by instructing the compiler to optimize cold and uncovered
--- a/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn
+++ b/build/config/compiler/BUILD.gn
@@ -1229,6 +1229,14 @@
         ]
       } else {
         ldflags += [ "-Wl,-mllvm,-ml-inliner-model-selector=arm32-size" ]
+        if (zebkit_ml_inliner_cold_cutoff > 0) {
+          # zebkit: as on high-end Android, the size model only where the
+          # caller is cold; and cold as zebkit_ml_inliner_cold_cutoff says.
+          ldflags += [
+            "-Wl,-mllvm,-ml-inliner-skip-policy=if-caller-not-cold",
+            "-Wl,-mllvm,-profile-summary-cutoff-cold=$zebkit_ml_inliner_cold_cutoff",
+          ]
+        }
       }
     }
   }
